1
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:05,510
[Dr Vincent Magombe, historian]
The first firing squad
that happened in 1972,

2
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:09,330
which I, for one, as a
young person in Uganda,

3
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:13,130
witnessed, we had never
seen anything like that.

4
00:02:44,367 --> 00:02:52,257
[Idi Amin]
This is not against Britain at all, it is
only transferring the economy to the hands

5
00:02:52,287 --> 00:02:53,497
of Ugandans.

6
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,130
[Idi Amin]
We have opened the fund.

7
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:09,600
He has saved the British fund by donating
10,000 shilling from my own saving.

8
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:49,290
[Ilan Hartuv, passenger on the hijacked flight]
Suddenly, we heard on the intercom a man
speaking in English with a German accent

9
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,700
who said that we've changed directions.

10
00:05:55,733 --> 00:06:03,467
[Wycliffe Kato, air traffic controller]
In the evening at eight, the soldiers
came and started beating me up.

11
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:13,490
[Major Iain Grahame, King's African Rifles]
There was a lot of bluff
and so on, you know.

12
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,750
We'll still defeat them.

13
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:21,670
And I've got battalions behind me and
everybody in the country is loyal to me.

14
00:07:21,860 --> 00:07:23,410
There was no truth to it at all.

15
00:07:23,440 --> 00:07:24,600
He knew his days were numbered.
